    ListNode<T>* curr = head;
    ListNode<T>* next = nullptr;

    while (curr != nullptr) {
        next = curr->next;
        curr->next = prev;
        prev = curr;
        curr = next;
    }

    return prev;
}
```

The `reverseList` function iterates through the linked list, reversing the direction of the pointers. It maintains three pointers: `prev` to keep track of the previous node, `curr` to keep track of the current node, and `next` to keep track of the next node. By reversing the pointers, the function effectively reverses the linked list and returns the new head.

